\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Jesus is alive and death is conquered
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  He has risen from the grave;
\par  Satan's  mighty forces are defeated,
\par  Now is Jesus strong to save.
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  O death where is your victory?
\par  What can the grave do? What can it do to me?
\par  For Christ has risen from death's prison,
\par  God has spoken, hell is broken,
\par   And my Lord has set me free!
\par \i0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Now I do not fear to cross the river:
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj  I know why my Saviour died!
\par  Even though the crossing may be painful
\par  He is on the other side.
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  O death where is your victory?
\par  What can the grave do? What can it do to me?
\par  For Christ has risen from death's prison,
\par  God has spoken, hell is broken,
\par   And my Lord has set me free!
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\i0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Praise his name with shouts of acclamation
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Our salvation now is sure!
\par  He came back to give us all this blessing:
\par  "Peace be with you evermore!"
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  O death where is your victory?
\par  What can the grave do? What can it do to me?
\par  For Christ has risen from death's prison,
\par  God has spoken, hell is broken,
\par   And my Lord has set me free!
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\i0 
\par \pard\f1 
